Z||000012||Old Lar||10-17-2000||08:20 PM||||That why there are lots of Fiero shows around the country.  The FOCOA national was in Louisville area.  Next year its in Williamsburg Va.  East coast attraction, long drive from Kansas.<P>There are regional shows in Florida in March, and one in Wisconsin the first week in June. In Michigan in mid June.  Long drive from Kansas.<P>The idea of the shows is a great one..putting one on is the biggest pain in the butt.  Just try to plan for one.<P>I've been going all over the country for Fiero shows for several years.  Too many complaints..you mean I have to drive more than 50 miles, I have to pay for a hotel, I can't get that much time off. ETC, ETC.<P>A hotel room costs $60-$85 a night for a moderate room.  Few will drive two days for a one day show.  Kansas although centrally located, will have to have some other attractions to bring out owners with their significant other.  You'll need to reserve lots of space for hotel rooms and overflow rooms.  You will hope that many will pre register to get an idea of head count.  You will discover that few will preregister and you'll have to guess head count. WhatthehellisinWichita?<P>Don't get me wrong I drove to KC this year in my Fiero..great barbeque.  Smokestack of Martin City.  KC is a long two day drive for me.  Florida is a long two day drive for me, Wisconsin is a long two day drive for me.  Any large show in the midwest will require a seven day commitment for me..two days out, two days back, three day show.  $500+ for hotels, gas, food etc I'm looking at $1000 for the trip.<P>Unless you are real good a planning large events, try to tag on to one of the regional shows or the national shows.  The regional shows will like the increase in show response as would the national club.  ||||reg||3
Z||000013||2xsess||10-17-2000||08:21 PM||||That would be awesome. Hopefully I'll have mine painted after I get back from Kosovo<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000014||Chris Schaefer||10-17-2000||09:26 PM||||Lar you are 1000% correct.  <P>With regards to the FOCOA National Festival, year 2001 is in Williamsburg, VA but 2002 is planned for Lake of the Ozarks, MO.  You can't get much more central than that.<P>Jeff your idea is good but there is no easier way than to all plan on the FOCOA Nationals.  Most of those who go have never heard of this forum.  Also there are several local club shows around the country all year long that all you have to do is pick one.||||reg||6
Z||000015||fieroparts.com||10-17-2000||09:46 PM||||old lar and chris,<P>You are  both 100000000000000000000%<BR>on the money. I have see this many times<BR>over the past 6 years planning shows.<BR>If I listed them all this post would be<BR>1000 lines long.<P>I will be at next years FOCOA show with<BR>my 1988 GT with org. T-Tops loaded...<BR>and only 117 miles yes 117 miles and I will be towing my baby.<P>FOCONE will be doing a caravan to the <BR>FOCOA and Michigan shows next year, more info to follow<BR>come||||reg||1
Z||000016||mrfiero||10-17-2000||10:05 PM||||Hey, no fair having fewer miles than me!!!<P>I guess I won't bring my "high" mileage Formula to the nationals this year (232 miles).   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Virginia is just too far for me to tow it, so I'll have to be content in driving my '88 GT there.  <P>I will definitely be bringing my Formula to the nationals in Missouri....finally a Fiero show that's less than a days drive from Denver!  Imagine that. ||||reg||4
